// mecatl driver API: the remote memory-store protocol.
//
// MemoryStoreService is the wire seam behind the harness's `tool.MemoryStore`
// (engine/tool/tool.go): an operator-run driver process holds the
// cross-session ("tiered") memory entries in place of the in-process flock
// store (internal/adapter/memory). The driver sits at the SAME trust tier as
// an on-disk memory directory — operator-configured infrastructure, not a
// model-facing surface. Sanitization of model-written values stays
// HARNESS-SIDE (the memory tools); a driver is never trusted to sanitize.
//
// The six RPCs mirror the tool.MemoryStore interface one-for-one. Behavioral
// contract (pinned by the engine/adapter/memconformance suite, which remote
// drivers run over their client):
//   - RememberEntry overwrites by key and bumps updated_at; a blank or
//     whitespace-only key is INVALID_ARGUMENT.
//   - Recall of a missing key is found=false — NEVER NOT_FOUND.
//   - List/Index results are key-sorted; Search is best-first and
//     deterministic for identical store state and query.
//   - Index/Search results OMIT values (the tier-0 routing table); List and
//     Recall return them.
//   - Forget of a missing key succeeds (idempotent).
//
// Validation: required-field annotations are authored with `buf.validate.field`
// for documentation and future runtime enforcement; V1 enforces them in the Go
// client/server wrappers (internal/adapter/grpcdriver).

